WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.504
Incompetence is an alibi.

00:00:02.454 --> 00:00:08.806
The Institutional Malice Doctrine is the thesis that Canada's political failures are not accidental — they are willful.

00:00:08.806 --> 00:00:12.340
Every pattern, once examined, reveals a choice.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:14.068
Not a mistake.

00:00:14.068 --> 00:00:15.579
A decision.

00:00:15.579 --> 00:00:18.409
Evidence block one: ArriveCAN.

00:00:18.409 --> 00:00:21.113
Ninety-three million dollars wasted.

00:00:21.113 --> 00:00:24.738
Every Liberal MP voted against recovering the funds.

00:00:24.738 --> 00:00:27.136
Evidence block two: MAID.

00:00:27.136 --> 00:00:31.102
One point two seven three trillion dollars in projected savings.

00:00:31.102 --> 00:00:37.931
Evidence block three: the Canadian Armed Forces — twelve thousand, seven hundred and eighty-five troop shortfall.

00:00:37.931 --> 00:00:43.840
Evidence block four: foreign interference — zero registrations under the transparency registry.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:49.590
The UN Committee on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities demanded MAID repeal — the government ignored it.

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:54.818
The RCMP closed the Chinese police station investigation with zero charges.

00:00:54.818 --> 00:00:59.727
CFNIS whistleblowers were prosecuted with twenty-eight charges while abusers were protected.

00:00:59.727 --> 00:01:03.477
At what point does a pattern of inaction become a policy of harm?
